the puja 108 is especially popular with  female drivers it comes as a three or  five-door hatchback and there are all  sorts of exterior paintwork and interior  choices if you shell out 1250 euros more  you can get a retractable fabric roof  that provides a nice breeze on a sunny  day test driver  eNOS Petrie says she's testing the  three-door version of the top  convertible she's especially interested  in how much space there is whichever  version of the 108 you go for the  dimensions are the same and there are  many reasons why this small french car  is a runner with women the paintwork can  be purple if desired the fabric roof can  be black gray or purple there's a makeup  mirror above the driver's seat but is  the car family-friendly  Athena says a modern woman has to juggle  various tasks in her daily routine  there are easel fix anchors on the back  seat to attach a child seat though it  might be a tight fit this would be  easier with four doors but the test car  only has three and that is often the  case in the real world too often people  buy these cars before they have kids and  then they have to adapt there isn't that  much extra space left over if the  driver's seat is pushed forward but it  is easy enough to install a child seat  Tina says that although you can put a  seat in it could get a bit fiddly to put  on seat belts she says people who are  thinking of using the car with kids  would be better off investing in two  extra doors the five-door version would  be more compatible with extra adults -  on the road the puja 108's performance  is very good it's capable of reaching a  maximum top speed of 170 km/h and  consumes 4.3 litres of gasoline per 100  kilometres this means  co2 emissions are kept below the 100  gram market the basic three door model  without a fabric roof cost less than  nine thousand euros in Germany  EDA says that the Peugeot 108 only  offers three cylinder engines this one  has 60 kilowatts that's more than enough  for city driving you can keep up with  the traffic and never get a feeling of  falling behind the 108 is very modern  when it comes to communications  she says the white interior reminds her  of modern tablet computers and the  technology in the car is just as modern  you could connect your phone to the cars  display and navigate via the phone for  example but if you haven't planned the  route in advance it consumes a lot of  data that's why young drivers might want  to resort to a traditional navigation  system  if a car is shorter than three and a  half meters long  you can't expect that much from the  trunk but this one is fine for shopping  in town possum you can fold down the  rear seats for more story space a total  of 780 liters if you have a child and a  bit more stuff you might have to be  creative about how to use the space  available if there's a child seat in  place you can only pull down one  backseat there's space for the shopping  but you might be a bit hard pressed if  you also wanted to fit in a buggy the  five-door hatchback might not provide  any more space but when it comes to  comfort and convenience it's definitely  worth shelling out the extra 450 euros  you
 

